From: SaaiOS <os@saaios>
Subject: synaptics td4150: only clear stale plen on STATUS_OK drained frames

v019 since11: payload_fully_drained was set for every continued_read with
rem=0, including async REPORT_IDENTIFY (0x10) frames. read_message then
zeroed plen on those reports, corrupting probe/identify and preventing
ENABLE_REPORT from ever running (dmesg shows only one early continued_read).

Fix:
1. Set payload_fully_drained only when status_report_code == STATUS_OK.
2. Zero stale plen in read_message only when drained && STATUS_OK.
3. Log probe milestone before touch_init.

Applies after syna-tcm-read-message-plen-zero.patch.

--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics/td4150/synaptics_tcm_core.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics/td4150/synaptics_tcm_core.c
@@ -817,8 +817,11 @@ static int syna_tcm_continued_read(struct syna_tcm_hcd *tcm_hcd)
 			tcm_hcd->status_report_code == STATUS_CONTINUED_READ)
 		tcm_hcd->status_report_code = STATUS_OK;
 
-	if (remaining_length == 0)
+	/* Only mark transport-complete for STATUS_OK chains. Async reports
+	 * (e.g. REPORT_IDENTIFY 0x10) also end with rem=0 but must keep plen.
+	 */
+	if (remaining_length == 0 &&
+			tcm_hcd->status_report_code == STATUS_OK)
 		tcm_hcd->payload_fully_drained = true;
 
 	pr_info("SAaiOS_TOUCH_DBG: continued_read exit status=0x%02x plen=%u bytes_read=%u rem=%u chunks=%u drained=%d\n",
@@ -1152,11 +1155,12 @@ static int syna_tcm_read_message(struct syna_tcm_hcd *tcm_hcd,
 
 	LOCK_BUFFER(tcm_hcd->in);
 
-	/* continued_read may finish with rem=0 while header plen is still the
-	 * original multi-chunk size; check_padding uses total_length derived
-	 * from plen and would otherwise probe past in.buf → -EIO (rc=-5).
+	/* continued_read may finish STATUS_OK with rem=0 while header plen still
+	 * shows the original multi-chunk size; check_padding would otherwise
+	 * probe past in.buf. Do not clear plen on async reports (0x10 etc.).
 	 */
-	if (tcm_hcd->payload_fully_drained)
+	if (tcm_hcd->payload_fully_drained &&
+			tcm_hcd->status_report_code == STATUS_OK)
 		tcm_hcd->payload_length = 0;
 
 	total_length = MESSAGE_HEADER_SIZE + tcm_hcd->payload_length + 1;
@@ -3794,6 +3798,9 @@ static int syna_tcm_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	syna_tcm_attn_clear_pending(tcm_hcd);
 
+	pr_info("SAaiOS_TOUCH_DBG: probe before touch_init mode=0x%02x app_info_sent=%d\n",
+		tcm_hcd->id_info.mode, tcm_hcd->app_info_cmd_sent ? 1 : 0);
+
 	/* initialize the touch reporting */
 	retval = touch_init(tcm_hcd);
 	if (retval < 0) {
